# Legends of the Twins — new feats, pp.12-13. The book (p.12) says its versions are more current than Age of Mortals' and War of the Lance's where they differ.
Academic Priest	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:Your path to faith is more scholarly than other clerics'.	BENEFIT:For bonus divine spells per day and maximum divine spell level, your primary spellcasting ability is Intelligence. With more than one divine spellcasting class, it applies to only one of them. Your spell save DCs do not change. Special: You may take this feat only as a 1st-level character. Taken again, it applies to a different divine spellcasting class. You may take it with no divine spellcasting class yet.	PRESTAT:1,INT=13	PRETEXT:Intelligence 13	SOURCEPAGE:p.12
Alternate Form	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You can assume an animal or humanoid form, as a silver, gold or bronze dragon can.	BENEFIT:Once per day, assume one specific alternate humanoid or animal form of Medium size or smaller. This works as a polymorph spell cast on yourself at your caster level, except that you regain no hit points for changing. You may stay in the form until you choose to return to your natural form. Special: May be taken more than once; each time adds one change of form per day. Silver, gold and bronze dragons with this feat may change form one additional time each day.	PRETEXT:Dragon, adult age or older, caster level 5th	SOURCEPAGE:p.12
Astrological Forecasting	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You read the heavens for insight into your fate.	BENEFIT:Once a week, prepare a reading: an hour with a view of the night sky and a Knowledge (arcana) check. DC 20 partial reading, +1 bonus; DC 25 complete, +2; DC 30 superlative, +3. The bonus is an insight bonus on any one ability check, skill check, attack roll, saving throw or initiative roll in the next seven days. You may prepare a reading for a character you know: you choose the type of check, they choose when to use it. Special: The type of check is chosen when the reading is prepared; the bonus may be used any time before the week is up. If it goes unused, no reading may be prepared the following week.	PRESKILL:1,Knowledge (Arcana)=4	PRETEXT:Knowledge (arcana) 4 ranks	SOURCEPAGE:p.12
Charming	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:Others find your company appealing.	BENEFIT:+2 on Diplomacy and Bluff checks.	BONUS:SKILL|Diplomacy,Bluff|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.12
Disciplined	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You keep your composure even when your life is threatened.	BENEFIT:+1 on Will saves and +2 on Concentration checks.	BONUS:SAVE|Will|1	BONUS:SKILL|Concentration|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.12
Dynamic Priest	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:Your self-confidence and force of personality are the foundation of your faith.	BENEFIT:For bonus divine spells per day and maximum divine spell level, your primary spellcasting ability is Charisma. With more than one divine spellcasting class, it applies to only one of them. Your spell save DCs do not change. Special: You may take this feat only as a 1st-level character. Taken again, it applies to a different divine spellcasting class. You may take it with no divine spellcasting class yet.	SOURCEPAGE:p.12
Education	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You had several years of formal schooling and were an excellent student.	BENEFIT:All Knowledge skills are class skills for you, whatever your class. +2 on two Knowledge skills of your choice. Special: You may take this feat only as a 1st-level character.	CSKILL:TYPE=Knowledge	PRETEXT:Civilized human, half-elf, Silvanesti elf or Qualinesti elf	SOURCEPAGE:p.12
Haggler	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You are skilled at brokering business deals.	BENEFIT:+2 on all Appraise and Bluff checks.	BONUS:SKILL|Appraise,Bluff|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.12
Heroic Surge	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You draw on inner reserves to act more in a round.	BENEFIT:Take an additional move or attack action, before or after your regular actions. Uses per day by character level: 1st-4th once; 5th-8th twice; 9th-12th three times; 13th-16th four times; 17th-20th five times. Never more than once per round.	SOURCEPAGE:p.12-13
Improved Taunt	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You are skilled at enraging others with insults and jeering.	BENEFIT:On a successful Bluff check against the target's Sense Motive check, the target takes -2 on attack rolls and AC, and its attitude shifts two steps toward hostile (DMG Chapter 4, NPC attitudes). The taunt lasts rounds equal to your Charisma bonus, twice that if the Bluff check beats the Sense Motive by 10 or more; it works once per encounter. Instead of one target you may taunt a crowd: a Bluff check against DC 10 + 1 per 2 targets shifts their attitude one step toward hostile, with no penalty to attacks or AC. Special: Close friends and long-time acquaintances of the target gain a +4 morale bonus to resist the taunt if targeted.	PRESTAT:1,CHA=13	PRETEXT:Charisma 13, Taunt exceptional ability	SOURCEPAGE:p.13
Lucky	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You survive through sheer good fortune.	BENEFIT:+1 luck bonus on all saving throws.	BONUS:SAVE|ALL|1|TYPE=Luck	SOURCEPAGE:p.13
Mimic	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You have a natural talent for impersonation.	BENEFIT:+2 on Disguise and Perform checks.	BONUS:SKILL|Disguise,TYPE.Perform|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.13
Quick-Thinking	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You react quickly to danger.	BENEFIT:+2 on initiative rolls and +2 on all Spot checks.	BONUS:COMBAT|INITIATIVE|2	BONUS:SKILL|Spot|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.13
Sharp-Eyed	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You have an eye for small details.	BENEFIT:+2 on Search and Sense Motive checks.	BONUS:SKILL|Search,Sense Motive|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.13
Spellcasting Prodigy	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You have an exceptional gift for magic.	BENEFIT:For bonus spells per day, treat your primary spellcasting ability score as 2 points higher than it is. With more than one spellcasting class, it applies to only one of them. Special: You may take this feat only as a 1st-level character. Taken again (for example, as a human), it applies to a different spellcasting class. You may take it with no spellcasting class yet.	SOURCEPAGE:p.13
Street Smart	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You stay informed and keep an ear to the ground without raising suspicion.	BENEFIT:+2 on all Bluff and Gather Information checks.	BONUS:SKILL|Bluff,Gather Information|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.13
Stubborn	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You are headstrong, and hard to sway from your course.	BENEFIT:+1 on Will saves and +2 on Intimidate checks.	BONUS:SAVE|Will|1	BONUS:SKILL|Intimidate|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.13
Trustworthy	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	DESC:You project a friendly demeanor.	BENEFIT:+2 on all Diplomacy and Gather Information checks.	BONUS:SKILL|Diplomacy,Gather Information|2	SOURCEPAGE:p.13
